    dcterms:source "NVIS Technical Working Group (2017) Australian Vegetation Attribute Manual: National Vegetation Information System, Version 7.0. Department of the Environment and Energy, Canberra. Prep by Bolton, M.P., deLacey, C. and Bossard, K.B. (Eds)." ;
    skos:definition "NVIS height class 2 comprises of vegetation heights in the range between 0.5 - 1 metre. These include growth forms such as low-shrub, heath shrub, chenopod shrub, ferns, samphire shrub, cycad, tree-fern, grass-tree and palm (multi-stemmed). They can also include some of the mid-tussock grass, hummock grass, other grass, sedge, rush, forbs, vine (G) and tall lower growth forms such as bryophytes, lichens and aquatic seagrass. " ;
    skos:notation "2" ;
    skos:note "NVIS height class 2 comprises of vegetation heights in the range between 0.5 - 1 metre. These include growth forms such as low-shrub, heath shrub, chenopod shrub, ferns, samphire shrub, cycad, tree-fern, grass-tree and palm (multi-stemmed). They can also include some of the mid-tussock grass, hummock grass, other grass, sedge, rush, forbs, vine (G) and tall lower growth forms such as bryophytes, lichens and aquatic seagrass. " ;
    skos:prefLabel "height class 2" ;
.

