    skos:definition "Mosses and Liverworts. Mosses are small plants usually with a slender leaf- bearing stem with no true vascular tissue. Liverworts are often moss-like in appearance or consisting of a flat, ribbon-like green thallus." ;
    skos:notation "B" ;
    skos:note "Mosses and Liverworts. Mosses are small plants usually with a slender leaf- bearing stem with no true vascular tissue. Liverworts are often moss-like in appearance or consisting of a flat, ribbon-like green thallus." ;
    skos:prefLabel "bryophyte" ;
.

