    skos:altLabel
        "Level 5" ,
        "vegetation association" ;
    skos:definition "Vegetation association is a member of the NVIS vegetation hierarchy that requires up to three up to three growth forms and three species in decreasing order of dominance for the three traditional strata. (i.e. Upper, Mid and Ground). Each stratum has a height and cover code. Nominate dominant stratum." ;
    skos:notation "5" ;
    skos:note "Vegetation association is a member of the NVIS vegetation hierarchy that requires up to three up to three growth forms and three species in decreasing order of dominance for the three traditional strata. (i.e. Upper, Mid and Ground). Each stratum has a height and cover code. Nominate dominant stratum." ;
    skos:prefLabel "association" ;
.

